{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding"]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLEndingV6Numbera","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"extendedModule":"IvorMXL","roleHeading":"Type Alias","symbolKind":"typealias","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Number","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Number","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLEnding.Number"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding\/Number-swift.typealias","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Number"},{"kind":"text","text":" = ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The ending-number type is used to specify the positive integers (without leading zeros) of the ending element.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"An empty array is used when software knows that an ending is present, but cannot determine the type of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ending.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlending\/number-swift.typealias"]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLEnding/Number-swift.typealias":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlending\/number-swift.typealias","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding\/Number-swift.typealias","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Number"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The ending-number type is used to specify the positive integers (without leading zeros) of the ending element.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"An empty array is used when software knows that an ending is present, but cannot determine the type of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ending.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Number","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLEnding.Number"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","title":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLEnding":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLEnding"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLEnding"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlending","abstract":[{"text":"The ending type represents multiple (e.g. first and second) endings. Typically, the start type is associated","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with the left barline of the first measure in an ending. The stop and discontinue types are associated with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the right barline of the last measure in an ending. Stop is used when the ending mark concludes with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"downward jog, as is typical for first endings. Discontinue is used when there is no downward jog, as is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"typical for second endings that do not conclude a piece. The length of the jog can be specified using the end-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"length attribute. The text-x and text-y attributes are offsets that specify where the baseline of the start of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the ending text appears, relative to the start of the ending line.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLEnding","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding","kind":"symbol"}}}